// differential: setup raster
// differential: across relative 0.05
// Screen-space derivatives of what is linear across the target, and of what bends, which a quad's coarse and fine differences tell apart.
// Across machines the bent value's derivative is coarse on one and fine on another until every target writes coarse (feat-sgl-coarse-derivatives-by-default).
// Metal's is fine under safe math and coarse under fast math, so the reference holds it loosely across machines and exactly across routes.
use diff_raster

@pixel fun derivatives_ps(p: diff_raster.varyings) -> diff_raster.target:
    let bent = p.weight * p.weight
    return {color = float4(ddx(p.weight), ddy(p.uv.y), ddx(bent) + ddy(bent), fwidth(p.uv.x * 7.0))}
